---
/**
 * The Tagaby band — a way to give by SHOPPING, not a sponsor.
 *
 * A sponsor gives money and is thanked with a logo; Tagaby is the other
 * direction, where families buy something and a share comes back. So it sits
 * with the ways to give and never on the sponsor wall, where it would read as
 * "this business donated" and sit paying sponsors beside a shop link.
 *
 * Its own deep-teal band for two reasons. On both pages that use it, it sits
 * directly above the sponsor section, which fills with --surface-sunken — the
 * fill this band used to share, so the two ran together as one block. And
 * Tagaby's wordmark is white, which is invisible on any light fill and needs a
 * dark one to be legible at all. Teal rather than maroon because this is PAC's,
 * and because the home page's ask above it is already maroon.
 *
 * One component rather than two copies: it appears on the home page and on
 * Support Us, and a second copy is how the event pages drifted before they were
 * pulled into one route.
 */
---

<section class="tagaby-band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tagaby-inner">
      <img class="tagaby-logo" src="/img/tagaby.png" alt="Tagaby" width="807" height="315" />
      <div class="tagaby-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">PAC &middot; A way to give</p>
        <h2>Help reduce Lost &amp; Found</h2>
        <p>Sundance donates nearly <b>800 unclaimed items</b> every year. Tagaby tags help
           them find their way home &mdash; and <b>20% of profits</b> comes back to the PAC.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-lg btn-primary" href="/tagaby/">How Tagaby works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
